=== ch4_packet
if p_kaye_reply == "unanswered":
    KAYE: You didn't answer my message. I thought you were busy.
    KAYE: I suppose you were.
    ~ kaye_mentioned_unanswered = true
SAL: Right. I've got a packet here with Ari's name on it, and I'd like to read it before anybody signs anything. I've been wanting to do that all week.
if jad_argue == "agreed" or jad_argue == "suspicious":
    JAD: Read the back.
    SAL: I'm going to read the back.
SAL: This is the ARP-2. Arrival and Responder Packet. Top sheet.
@show_doc arp2_top
@gallery_add arp2_top
SAL: One signature box. "Please sign to complete your registration."
* [ask] "What's underneath it?"
* [ask] "Can I see the back?"
SAL: It's a carbon set. Hang on.
SOUND: Paper, lifted by a corner. The squeak of carbon.
@show_doc arp2_under
@gallery_add arp2_under
~ k_carbon = true
SAL: Under the top sheet, two pages. The one box on top comes through on both.
SAL: Page one's the R-1 part. Registration of Arrival. Your name, a witness, the date. There's a box for body record. It's empty. It's never been filled in.
SAL: Page two's the RA-3. Appointment of Community Responder, Sole.
SAL: Sole designated responder for all forty-two households of Ferrier Court. Availability: continuous. Nine pounds sixty per hour of active response. Accommodation: Office G/1, charge applies.
SAL: On commencement, the Overnight Support Service will cease.
~ k_terms = true
NELL: Continuous? Like, all the time?
SAL: That's what continuous means.
TEODOR: Nine pounds sixty.
He says it like a man who was in the tramworkers' union for thirty-one years.
TEODOR: Per hour of active. What's active?
SAL: When you're responding. Not when you're waiting to.
TEODOR: That's not a wage. That's a tip.
KAYE: Well...
KAYE: If you're going to be here anyway, dear, Thursday...
She stops. Her hand goes to her mouth, not dramatically, just to hold it still.
KAYE: No. Listen to me.
~ kaye_caught_herself = true
* "Sign the top, you've signed all three?"
    SAL: Sign the top, you've signed all three. That's how they built it. It saves a column.
* "Can I sign just the first one?"
    SAL: Legally? Yes. Arrival registration's a right. The appointment's a job. Different Acts. Different decades.
    SAL: In practice, there's one box.
    ~ asked_sign_one = true
SAL: There's an old form. R-1. Registration of Arrival, on its own. I've got forty of them in a box in the cabinet in the lobby. Nobody uses them, because the system hasn't got a screen for them.
SAL: I'd have to key it by hand on Monday. I would, though.
@text_doc sal r1_standalone "The old one. And the bit on the box that matters. S."
~ k_r1 = true
SAL: I need an answer by half five. From Ari. Not from any of you.
SAL: And a witness, whatever it is. Somebody who'll put their name to having been there.
-> ch4_breakup

=== ch4_breakup
They go the way they came, in ones and twos. Chairs scrape. Mrs. Kaye takes her cushion. June leaves her flask on the tiles for whoever.
Nell stops at the ladder and looks down at the chair in the deep end for a while.
NELL: Night, Ari.
NELL: Morning. Whatever it is.
Inez climbs down. The phone lifts off the chair, swinging, and the room tilts in your sense of it, and she's got you under her arm like a parcel.
INEZ: Frame. Come on.
@state chairs off
~ gap_n = 4
->> tick_only
-> ch4_aftermath

